{
  "about": "The slice's twelve generic people's default days (M1 sprint 6, step 4; chapter 12, 3.1: stallholders, porters, elders on the barkor, children, two drovers; archetypes TM, TW, TE, TB, TG, CV, NW, HM), read by tools/town/graph.py into the street graph's walkers beside the named eight (data/named_days.json, whose form this is: each stop [place, arrive, leave, how, loops, seat] in game minutes from midnight). body is the figure (../tibet-blender/people2/body.py GENERIC); home a place, or near:<place>, the nearest house door to it that no other of them has. Seats as the named eight's, and spot:<east>:<north>[:<bearing>], metres from the place's anchor, facing a bearing clockwise from north (or the way it came); stall:<k>:<along>:front, before the k-th stall's counter, facing it. The drovers are at the camp (away past the Yak Gate) all day in TownSim's terms: world/caravan.gd places them with the caravan CV-02 from 14:55 (sprint 6, step 5). The three town houses to enter have their households at home (sprint 8, ISS-105): room:house_kitchen_b2_in_v<n>:seat:<k> is a seat in the kitchen of the house that is the stop's place. They sit cross-legged on their benches (how cross; ISS-088). The poor family's grandmother at H-SHL-142 on the west edge (chapter 04, 4.2) spins standing by her door all day and sits cross-legged by the fire from 17:30: room:house_room_e1_in_v<n>:spot:<x>:<y>[:<bearing>], metres into the room from the door's inner face (x along the door's wall), facing a bearing in it (0 in); her house was off the graph's ground until M2 sprint 6, step 2 (she now leaves it at dusk, below). The two novices (IMP-024, after Greg's 1776) come down the Sky Stair from its top in the afternoon, as chapter 05's novices with the reading party: one round the great wheel, the other to Dechen-tsang's gate, both to the boy's knucklebones on Tsongra, and back up before half past four. M2 sprint 6, step 2 (IMP-030): the ngakpa quarter's householders (two men in the tantric practitioners' white, to Pema Ö's service at 07:50; two women) round Pema Ö (pema_o, conch_terrace), and the west edge's poor family of H-SHL-142 (chapter 04, 4.2: Norbu to the Landing at 06:40 and Dawa out for water and dung by 06:00, by west_way, away; the eldest girl at the caravan ground; the boy by the west edge's lane and the western mani wall; the grandmother's lingkor on its west side at dusk, west_mani). M2 sprint 6, step 3 (chapter 05, A-47): the water carriers of upper Shöl, four women and two girls each with her barrel on her back (../tibet-blender people2/body.py), to the Lukhang spring (spring) and home again three times from 05:40 and twice from 15:30; at the spring world/spring.gd places them in the queue, at the spouts and behind the queue talking, from the moment they come in at its way in to the moment they leave it. M2 sprint 6, step 4 (chapter 08, V-13a): the old woman of upper Shöl who goes up the garden lane every dusk from H-SHL-095 at the lane's foot to burn juniper on the Gorge Rim Lookout's burner (lookout) and greet the god in the notch, home after dark.",
